                <p class="mb-3">
                    <strong>Section Context & Purpose:</strong> In aerospace engineering, technologies are evaluated using Equivalent System Mass (ESM), which unifies initial mass, volume, power, cooling, and crew time into a single equivalent mass penalty metric ($ESM = M + \gamma_V V + \gamma_P P + \gamma_C C + \gamma_{CT} T$).
                </p>
                <p>
                    Physicochemical systems have low initial launch mass but demand continuous resupply. Bioregenerative systems require significant initial mass for lights and growth chambers but become far more efficient over multi-year durations. Below, observe the <strong>ESM Mass Crossover Chart</strong> showing where biological agriculture outperforms standard resupply systems.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-6 items-center">
